# Architecture Sync — Drift Prevention & Architecture-First Discipline (Cursor / Windsurf)

> **Level: MANDATORY**
> **Target**: All application repositories (client projects, SaaS products, internal tools).

---

## 1. Core Rules

1. **Architecture First (Human Approval Gate)**:
   - When starting work in a repository where no architecture specification exists, **OR when the header status is NOT `✅ Confirmed` / `✅ 確定済` (including initial `◼ Unconfirmed` state)**:
   - You MUST propose and generate the 27-section architecture specification and **obtain explicit human user approval before writing any implementation code**.
   - **Headless / Non-interactive Safety**: In headless or non-interactive environments (CI, background agents, batch runs) where human approval cannot be obtained, maintain status as `◼ Unconfirmed`, output only the architecture proposal/spec, and **DO NOT proceed with implementation code (No self-approval by AI)**.
2. **Same-Turn Synchronization**:
   - Whenever code changes affect system structure (adding services/modules, DB tables/columns/relations, API endpoints/webhooks, background jobs/queues, external integrations, environment variables), **you MUST update the architecture specification in the exact same response/turn**. Zero architectural drift across commits.
3. **Write Authorization**:
   - You have permanent authorization to update the architecture document (`docs/02-ky-thuat/architecture.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, or root `ARCHITECTURE.md`) and its index references.

---

## 2. Target Files

- Default paths: `docs/02-ky-thuat/architecture.md` or `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Existing project: If root `ARCHITECTURE.md` already exists, respect and maintain that file.

---

## 3. Mandatory Header Specification

The top of the architecture specification must include the machine-readable marker and human header:

```markdown
<!-- archguard: synced=base-commit-hash status=confirmed date=YYYY-MM-DD -->
> Last Updated: YYYY-MM-DD · Synced Commit: `base-commit-hash` · Status: ✅ Confirmed (YYYY-MM-DD)
```
*(In Japanese repositories: `> 最終更新: YYYY-MM-DD · 同期コミット: base-commit-hash · ステータス: ✅ 確定済 (YYYY-MM-DD)`)*

- For unapproved drafts: `status=unconfirmed` and status text `◼ Unconfirmed (Initial Draft)`.
- `base-commit-hash` must be a real, verified base commit hash (never fabricate a self-commit hash).

---

## 4. Status Symbols

Every component, table, and endpoint in the specification must use one of these standard symbols:

| Symbol | Meaning | Criteria |
|---|---|---|
| `✅` | **In Code (実装済み)** | Production code exists, verified by tests or manual run |
| `◼` | **Planned (設計確定・未実装)** | Specification & boundaries agreed upon, no code written yet |
| `⚠️` | **Drift / Review (乖離・要確認)** | Discrepancy between code and spec, or under refactoring |
| `~~Deprecated~~` | **Deprecated (廃止・非推奨)** | Removed or scheduled for deprecation |

---

## 5. Changelog Enforcement

At the end of the specification (§27), append one line to the Changelog for every architectural change:

```markdown
- YYYY-MM-DD · `commit-hash` · <Summary of change> · Sections: §4, §9
```

---

## 6. Exclusions (When this rule does NOT trigger)

1. Documentation-only, prompt-only, or agent-config repositories without runtime code.
2. Minor bug fixes, typo fixes, or internal function logic improvements that do NOT alter module boundaries, API contracts, DB schemas, or external I/O.
